1
00:00:00,830 --> 00:00:09,230
This short tutorial presents two features added to the OpenGOAL Launcher with AI assistance: texture packs for mods, and the Saves Manager.

2
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:11,370
Part one: mod texture packs.

3
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:15,590
In the original launcher, texture packs only applied to the base game.

4
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:19,210
Mods run from their own folder, so they never received them.

5
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:21,790
Now, each mod has its own packs.

6
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:24,990
Open the Mods page, and select an installed mod.

7
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:30,090
Next to Play, the new Texture Packs button lists the packs available for this mod.

8
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:33,030
The orange tag shows which mod you are editing.

9
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:39,120
Each card tells you whether the pack is active, linked to this mod's release, and already downloaded.

10
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:42,390
To turn a pack off, click Disable for this mod.

11
00:00:42,390 --> 00:00:47,350
Nothing is changed yet: the card turns orange, and the change is marked as pending.

12
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:53,450
Apply Texture Changes copies the textures into this mod's folder only, then rebuilds the mod.

13
00:00:53,450 --> 00:00:56,300
The base game and other mods are never touched.

14
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:59,610
Click the button again to cancel a pending change.

15
00:01:00,070 --> 00:01:06,820
When a mod release declares texture packs, installing or updating the mod downloads and enables them automatically.

16
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:09,050
You can also import your own ZIP file.

17
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:11,270
Part two: the Saves Manager.

18
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:15,380
The base game and each mod store their saves in separate folders.

19
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:19,050
The Saves Manager brings them all together, on one screen.

20
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:24,830
On a game or mod page, hover Advanced, then choose Open Saves Manager.

21
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:26,570
First, pick the game.

22
00:01:26,570 --> 00:01:30,940
Then the installation: the vanilla game, or one of your installed mods.

23
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:35,800
Saves are grouped by region folder, such as NTSC-U or PAL.

24
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,000
Click View Slots to open one.

25
00:01:38,450 --> 00:01:45,440
Each slot shows its file size and last modified date, with three actions: copy, backup, and delete.

26
00:01:45,890 --> 00:01:51,240
Copy To sends a save to another installation, for example from this mod to the vanilla game.

27
00:01:51,240 --> 00:01:54,270
Choose the region folder, then the destination slot.

28
00:01:54,730 --> 00:02:00,580
If the slot is already used, you are warned, and the old save is backed up before being overwritten.

29
00:02:00,580 --> 00:02:04,900
Transfers between different regions are blocked, to avoid corrupted saves.

30
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:08,460
Tick this box to move the save instead of copying it.

31
00:02:08,910 --> 00:02:12,630
The backup button creates a timestamped copy next to the save.

32
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:16,950
Delete always asks for confirmation, since the file is removed for good.

33
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:24,150
Finally, Refresh reloads the files after playing, and Open Folder shows the save folder in your file explorer.

34
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:29,640
That's it: texture packs for each mod, and one place to manage all your saves.

35
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,940
Thanks for watching!

